Apple could capture nearly 30% of the global foldable smartphone market in 2027, according to <a href="https://www.trendforce.com/presscenter/news/20261028-13282.html">TrendForce's latest forecast</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-dark.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072436" /><br/>
TrendForce projects Apple's share of shipments rising from 24.8% in 2026 to 29.8% in 2027. Samsung is expected to retain first place, although its share is forecast to fall from 35.1% to 31.9%. Huawei would follow Apple in third place, with its share declining from 24.8% to 21.3%. The research firm estimates approximately five million <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> shipments in 2026, while overall foldable smartphone shipments are expected to grow just 0.5%.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/trendforce-iphone-duo-foldable-market-2024-2027.jpg" alt="" width="1080" height="560" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075395" /><br/>
TrendForce says early feedback on the device has been mixed, with users praising <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/how-to/iphone-duo-open-two-apps-side-by-side/">split-screen functionality</a> and the viewing experience when the device is unfolded. However, some apps <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-support-app-iphone-duo/">display black borders</a> or fail to use the full screen, while reports of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/iphone-duo-crack-apple-response/">damaged displays</a> and high repair estimates have drawn attention to ownership costs.<br/>
<br/>
